.TH SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DUCK_OTHERS 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DUCK_OTHERS \- Specify whether this audio stream should duck other audio.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_hints.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_HINT_AUDIO_DUCK_OTHERS \(dqSDL_AUDIO_DUCK_OTHERS\(dq
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
On Apple platforms, this hint controls whether other audio streams are ducked (reduced in volume) while your application is in the foreground\[char46]
.PP
The variable can be set to the following values:
.PP

\(bu \(dq0\(dq: Other audio will not be ducked\[char46] (default)
.PP
\(bu \(dq1\(dq: Other audio will be ducked\[char46]
.PP
This hint should be set before an audio device is opened\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This hint is available since SDL 3\[char46]6\[char46]0\[char46]

